      "writtenOn": "2018-11-20T19:12:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What is the purpose of adding eid in UiccSlot? Is it the intention for callers to query eid from UiccSlot instead of EuiccCard? That may cause issues for old version. Because before HAL 1.3, there will be no EID in the slot / card status, so this filed will always be null, but actually inside EuiccCard, we will have real eid, and that is the value we want to use. In summary I don\u0027t think we want to add this field in UiccSLot",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 66,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 66,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "c644613d67abd3a47409cc0169d48dbbd9cdc155",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "843e5b19_b5c5d0d3",
        "filename": "src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/uicc/UiccSlot.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 66,
      "author": {
        "id": 1121198
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-11-20T19:36:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "EuiccCard is only created when we have cardstate, which I believe means that for an inactive eUICC we don\u0027t create an EuiccCard. However, we\u0027d like to be able to know whether a cardId corresponds to an eUICC even if the eUICC isn\u0027t active currently, so if we store the EID in UiccSlot, which always exists, we can do the lookup easily.\n\nAlso, though EID isn\u0027t always known, neither is ICCID and we already have mIccId in UiccSlot.\n\nAlternatively, if we really can\u0027t have EID here, we could not offer the ability to know if a cardId corresponds to an eUICC.\n\nWDYT?",
      "parentUuid": "7bdf4527_c7435a7e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 66,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 66,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "c644613d67abd3a47409cc0169d48dbbd9cdc155",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7331455f_d91270c6",
        "filename": "src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/uicc/UiccSlot.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 66,
      "author": {
        "id": 1148298
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-11-20T23:31:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I understand your intention to include the eid in UICC slot, but I still have the concern. EID is different from ICCID, ICCID is available in both slot / card status, so the ICCID will be updated in both Slot and Card, whenever there is status update. But for EID, when HAL \u003c 1.3, it is not available in slot / card status, we can only read it inside EuiccCard. So for all the devices running on HAL 1.2 and earlier, the eid in UiccSlot is always null but in EuiccCard it is not null, no matter the eUICC is enabled or not. How are you going to handle this inconsistency?",
      "parentUuid": "843e5b19_b5c5d0d3",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 66,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 66,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "c644613d67abd3a47409cc0169d48dbbd9cdc155",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "87f000c0_b2790e99",
        "filename": "src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/uicc/UiccSlot.java",
